    "detailed_description": "<h1>See also</h1><p><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.poster.avif?t=1647053826\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.webm?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.mp4?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1>Build musical scales <strong>easily</strong> with this <strong>minimalist puzzle game</strong>. Designed for music theory students of <strong>all levels</strong> (if you know the rules about building scales you're on):<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.poster.avif?t=1647053826\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.webm?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.mp4?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Featuring</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 11 different types of scales to train (from major to phrygian scales)<br></li><li> More than <strong>150 scales</strong> to build<br></li><li> Easy to play: drag the <strong>card</strong> to the <strong>blank spot</strong> and <strong>test the scale</strong><br></li><li> Music theory accuracy: You can apply the <strong>scale building</strong> here <strong>in real life</strong><br></li><li> Simple and <strong>minimalist</strong> art<br></li><li> Support for <strong>letter and syllabic notations</strong> for note names</li></ul><br>Do you have what it takes to build all scales?",
    "about_the_game": "Build musical scales <strong>easily</strong> with this <strong>minimalist puzzle game</strong>. Designed for music theory students of <strong>all levels</strong> (if you know the rules about building scales you're on):<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.poster.avif?t=1647053826\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.webm?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1753010/extras/dd9124abe6bf6bd35dcf2aaae8e252b0.mp4?t=1647053826\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Featuring</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 11 different types of scales to train (from major to phrygian scales)<br></li><li> More than <strong>150 scales</strong> to build<br></li><li> Easy to play: drag the <strong>card</strong> to the <strong>blank spot</strong> and <strong>test the scale</strong><br></li><li> Music theory accuracy: You can apply the <strong>scale building</strong> here <strong>in real life</strong><br></li><li> Simple and <strong>minimalist</strong> art<br></li><li> Support for <strong>letter and syllabic notations</strong> for note names</li></ul><br>Do you have what it takes to build all scales?",
